{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghc5QkSNqGpuahRyn4r7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XHtCXTguzHwqiTggXpcmHD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-h1db1_cb/NOTES.md","content":"# Ring classifier\n\n- **Layer 1 (32 units):** approximates each coordinate's square as a piecewise-linear function. For d in {0,1}, sign ±, and j=0..7, a unit computes relu(±x_d − j/8). Weighting these by h=1/8 (when j=0) or 2h (when j≥1) gives the linear interpolant of x_d² on the knots k/8. Its maximum error is h²/4 ≈ 0.004.\n- **Layer 2 (4 units used):** each unit reads s_hat = Σ coef·h1 ≈ x0²+x1². The thresholds are 0.16 and 0.5625, each shifted by the mean interpolation bias 2·h²/6 to compensate. The units are relu(s−a+e/2), relu(s−a−e/2), relu(s−b+e/2) and relu(s−b−e/2), with e=0.001.\n- **Output:** logit1 = (u1 − u2 − u3 + u4)/e is a trapezoid. It equals 1 for a ≤ s ≤ b and 0 outside, with ramps of width e. logit0 = 0.5. So the network predicts class 1 exactly when 0.4 ≤ r ≤ 0.75, apart from the small error of approximating r².\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3070,"cache_read_input_tokens":2254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3070},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1a9cddf-455c-4d8c-bc77-db1058bba66d","uuid":"1dffd483-e066-4cb8-a829-d6c1c6ae5f71","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:54:05.508Z","request_id":"req_011Cghc5QRqAd3wjeBXzLt61","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XHtCXTguzHwqiTggXpcmHD":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-h1db1_cb/NOTES.md","content":"# Ring classifier\n\n- **Layer 1 (32 units):** approximates each coordinate's square as a piecewise-linear function. For d in {0,1}, sign ±, and j=0..7, a unit computes relu(±x_d − j/8). Weighting these by h=1/8 (when j=0) or 2h (when j≥1) gives the linear interpolant of x_d² on the knots k/8. Its maximum error is h²/4 ≈ 0.004.\n- **Layer 2 (4 units used):** each unit reads s_hat = Σ coef·h1 ≈ x0²+x1². The thresholds are 0.16 and 0.5625, each shifted by the mean interpolation bias 2·h²/6 to compensate. The units are relu(s−a+e/2), relu(s−a−e/2), relu(s−b+e/2) and relu(s−b−e/2), with e=0.001.\n- **Output:** logit1 = (u1 − u2 − u3 + u4)/e is a trapezoid. It equals 1 for a ≤ s ≤ b and 0 outside, with ramps of width e. logit0 = 0.5. So the network predicts class 1 exactly when 0.4 ≤ r ≤ 0.75, apart from the small error of approximating r².\n"}}}
